# Send TP-Link firmware in recovery mode via TFTP
## 1. Install and config TFTP server
### 1.1 Install packages
`sudo apt update && sudo apt install tftp-hpa tftp`
### 1.2 Confirm TFTP config file
`sudo nano /etc/default/tftpd-hpa`
```Bash
TFTP_USERNAME="tftp"
TFTP_DIRECTORY="/var/lib/tftpboot" # Робоча папка
TFTP_ADDRESS="0.0.0.0:69"
TFTP_OPTIONS="--secure --ipv4 --blocksize 512" # 512 для стабільності
```
### 1.3 Set ownership and policy
```
sudo chown -R tftp:tftp /var/lib/tftpboot
sudo chmod -R 777 /var/lib/tftpboot
```
### 1.4 Restart TFTP service
`sudo service tftp-hpa restart`
## 2. Set network
### 2.1 Disable Firewall
`sudo ufw disable`
### 2.1 Set static IP for Ethernet device
`sudo ip addr add 192.168.0.100/24 dev enp0s25`
## 3. Prepare firwmare file 
### 3.1 Rename to wl or wl_rf.ko
`cp ./tp_link_firmware.bin ./wl`
### 3.2 Copy to TFTP files dir
`cp ./wl /var/lib/tftpboot`
## 4. Firmware update
### 4.1 Connect router by LAN1 or LAN4
### 4.2 Run monitoring
`sudo tcpdump -i enp0s25 -n udp port 69`
### 4.3 Set router in recovery mode
  * Push "Reset" button
  * Power up router and hold button 10-15 sec
  * Wait for "RRQ" in tcpdump (~5 min)
## 5. Check router after update
### 5.1 Connect to router via browser
`192.168.0.1` - for original TP-Link

`192.168.1.1` - for OpenWRT

